prompt_template:
The current directory is a checkout of the sem repository (Rust sources in a Cargo workspace under crates/). List every function that calls {target}, defined in {defined_in}. Other functions, methods and trait methods in the repository have the same name; calls to those are not calls of {target} and must not be listed. {count_rule} A function or method named as a value without being called (for example .map(Type::method)) and calls produced only by a macro's expansion do not count; calls written inside a macro's arguments (assert!, format!, vec!) do. Include callers in #[cfg(test)] modules, tests/, benches/ and examples/. For each call give the calling function (a method as Type::method, a free function as module::function; a call inside a closure belongs to the function the closure is written in), the file path relative to the repository root, and the 1-based line number of the call.

End your reply with a single JSON object and nothing after it:
{{"callers": [{{"method": "<Type>::<method>", "file": "crates/...", "line": 123}}]}}
